es being ported to the system we now  rejoice when they are I've already  mentioned the incredible bowel movement  inducing powers of doom but there's also  rocket League Bayonetta 1 &amp; 2  Mario Kart 8 Super Meat Boy and  Wolfenstein 2 the new Colossus just for  starters we've gotten to a point where  people are begging for games to be  released on the switch and for the first  time in a long while developers have a  good incentive to port their games to a  Nintendo console for example the indie  platformer Celeste was released on all  major platforms but the switch version  is currently outselling them all despite  having a smaller install base people are  seeing the switch as the best way to  play certain games and the portability  of the console is definitely a  contributing factor of course  portability might not apply to everyone  there are plenty of people who I'm sure  have no problem leaving their switch  nestled snugly in the dock with little  desire to take it anywhere and you know  what that's perfectly fine you can  choose to keep the console docked or  carry it around in your backpack because  that's the magic of the switch you  aren't constrained by any one form  factor you won't be handicapped if you  decide to take your switch on the go and  most importantly you can play it however  you want even if that means taking it to  the bathroom I hope you all enjoyed this  video I love my switch and I tend to  take it everywhere I go even if I don't  really use it it just kind of follows me  everywhere at this point but if you've  got any stories about you and your  switch or if you just want to scream  about how awesome it is feel free to put  it into the comments below we've been  doing videos this whole week celebrating  the switches first anniversary so make  sure you visit GameSpot comm to watch  all the other videos alright guys thanks  so much for watching and I'll see you  next time  [Music]

